<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bonds end lower, hurt by Italian BTP.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bonds end lower, hurt by Italian BTP.</headline>
<text>
<p>1810 GMT - Bonds ended weaker, hurt by the retreat of the Italian bonds (BTP). But the longer end continues more resilient than Spain due to a relative lack of paper. Short end supported. *March 97 futures down 10 basis points at 107.43 *Feb 07 cash 98.65 vs 98.70. *Spread vs Spanish 10-yr cash -16 bps vs -10 bps</p>
</text>
